# Cargo package: the sum is of Buildroot's vendored, re-packed archive
# (see bmcd.hash for the toolchain trap this shares).
#
# The version is commit 4009f9c on excavador-turing/tpi branch `hive`,
# released as v1.7.0: renaming a board no longer claims to move its metrics
# history, because the series never carried a board name.
#
# Bumped here because the firmware's own pin check caught it. The check
# reports on a PR and refuses on a tag, and it flagged tpi as stale the moment
# the interface was bumped -- which is exactly the drift it was written for,
# on its first real use.
#
# v1.7.0 -> v1.8.0 (b98c5079). `tpi health` and `tpi sdcard` reach the two
# endpoints the interface had to itself, the reboot help stops implying the
# compute modules go down with the daemon, and power status reads the
# daemon's "1"/"0" rather than parsing it as a number.
#
# THE RELEASE GATE IS WHY THIS IS HERE. v2.26.0 was tagged with tpi still at
# v1.7.0 and `tests/pins-are-current.sh` refused it: tpi 1.8.0 was published
# half an hour after firmware v2.25.0, so the pin was current when it was
# written and stale by the next release. That check is the only thing that
# noticed.
#
# Measured 2026-09-12 with the pinned container: `make tpi-source` reported
# got cc486206 against a zeroed expectation, then re-run to confirm it
# fetches and verifies cleanly.
sha256  cc48620669dd7d1802799fa46b1eb754e4e375583b43cc66026cbec70b705be7  tpi-b98c5079c1ed6a56e054b862d51049e25407ae4a-cargo2.tar.gz
sha256  a6cba85bc92e0cff7a450b1d873c0eaa2e9fc96bf472df0247a26bec77bf3ff9  LICENSE
